ssues.\n\n3. [MEDIUM] analyzeVideo — Video recording available (2m 55s). Analyze the video to extract visual context and user intents from the recording.\n\n4. [MEDIUM] getVideoChapters — AI-generated chapters are ready — a titled outline of the recording. Fetch the chapter list for a quick map of the recording before deciding where to look in the video, then call getFrames at a chapter's midpoint to see it.\n\n5. [MEDIUM] getUserEvents — 87 user interactions recorded. Review the sequence of clicks and inputs leading to the issue.\n\n6. [MEDIUM] getMetadata — Custom metadata attached to this Jam. Check custom metadata for application-specific context set by the developer.\n\nContext:\n- No description provided — visual and event data are the primary sources."}],"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"43f7895f-fb1a-482d-bdef-2df8db94ace7","session_id":"21880ebb-4ca2-4b72-9b3d-3b6dba0010a6","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/jvent/Dev/supabase/supabase-devtool","sessionId":"21880ebb-4ca2-4b72-9b3d-3b6dba0010a6","version":"2.1.266","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"2e58c991-4033-4a7b-b03c-f81d8821b41f","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[{"name":"mcp__claude_ai_Jam__analyzeVideo","description":"Extract user intents from a Jam recording. Identifies distinct user goals, issues, and feedback with detailed context including visual observations, interactions, and technical indicators.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"jamId":{"type":"string","description":"Jam identifier — a UUID or a jam.dev URL"}},"required":["jamId"],"additionalProperties":false,"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#"},"eager_input_streaming":true,"defer_loading":true},{"name":"mcp__claude_ai_Jam__getConsoleLogs","description":"Retrieve browser console output captured during the Jam session. Includes JavaScript errors, warnings, info messages, debug logs, and stack traces. Depending on the recording, the response is either a JSON envelope or plain newline-delimited JSON. The envelope form applies logLevel (an array — e.g. ['error','warn'] for problems) and limit server-side and reports `total` matching logs — if you get fewer than `total`, narrow the filter or page with `after`. In the newline-delimited form only `limit` applies; other parameters are ignored. Critical for identifying runtime errors, debugging application state issues, and understanding the sequence of events leading to bugs.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"jamId":{"type":"string","description":"Jam identifier — a UUID or a jam.dev URL"},"logLevel":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string","enum":["error","warn","info","debug"]},"description":"Optional filter by log levels, e.g. ['error','warn'] for problems."},"limit":{"type":"number","description":"Maximum number of events to return"},"after":{"type":"number","description":"Page cursor — pass the `nextCursor` from a previous response to continue"}},"required":["jamId"],"additionalProperties":false,"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#"},"eager_input_streaming":true,"defer_loading":true},{"name":"mcp__claude_ai_Jam__getDetails","description":"Retrieve comprehensive metadata and details for a specific Jam bug report. Returns essential information including: unique identifiers, author details, description, timestamps (created/updated), type (video/screenshot), and associated metadata. This is the primary entry point for analyzing any Jam - always call this tool first to understand the context before using other tools.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"jamId":{"type":"string","description":"Jam identifier — a UUID or a jam.dev URL"}},"required":["jamId"],"additionalProperties":false,"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#"},"eager_input_streaming":true,"defer_loading":true},{"name":"mcp__claude_ai_Jam__getNetworkRequests","description":"Extract network activity logs captured during the Jam session. Returns HTTP/HTTPS requests and WebSocket frames including: URLs, methods (GET/POST/etc), status codes, headers, payloads, response times, and error details. Depending on the recording, the response is either a JSON envelope or plain newline-delimited JSON. The envelope form applies filters server-side — each is an array, values OR within a filter, filters AND across: statusCode (e.g. ['4xx','5xx'] for all failures), contentType, host, method (e.g. ['POST','PUT'] for mutations), plus limit and after (page cursor) — and reports `total` matching events (if you get fewer, narrow the filter or page with `after`), and by default carries response bodies only for FAILED requests: pass bodies:'all' when you need the payload of a request that succeeded but returned the wrong data (bodies truncated to 4KB, flagged per row). In the newline-delimited form only `limit` applies; other parameters are ignored. Essential for debugging API issues, failed requests, CORS problems, and performance bottlenecks.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"jamId":{"type":"string","description":"Jam identifier — a UUID or a jam.dev URL"},"statusCode":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"description":"Filter by status codes and/or classes, e.g. ['500'] or ['4xx','5xx'] for all failures"},"contentType":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"description":"Filter by content-type substrings, e.g. ['application/json']"},"host":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"description":"Filter by host substrings, e.g. ['api.example.com']"},"method":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"description":"Filter by HTTP methods, e.g. ['POST','PUT','PATCH','DELETE'] for mutations"},"limit":{"type":"number","description":"Maximum number of events to return"},"after":{"type":"number","description":"Page cursor — pass the `nextCursor` from a previous response to continue"},"bodies":{"type":"string","enum":["errors","all"],"description":"Which response bodies to include. 'errors' (default) returns bodies only for failed requests; 'all' returns every body. Both are truncated to 4KB per body."}},"required":["jamId"],"additionalProperties":false,"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#"},"eager_input_streaming":true,"defer_loading":true},{"name":"mcp__claude_ai_Jam__getScreenshots","description":"Retrieve visual screenshots and image attachments from screenshot-type Jams. Returns image data that can be analyzed for UI issues, visual bugs, layout problems, or design inconsistencies. Note: This tool only works with Jams of type 'screenshot' - use getDetails first to verify Jam type.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"jamId":{"type":"string","description":"Jam identifier — a UUID or a jam.dev URL"}},"required":["jamId"],"additionalProperties":false,"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#"},"eager_input_streaming":true,"defer_loading":true},{"name":"mcp__claude_ai_Jam__getUserEvents","description":"Access the complete timeline of user interactions captured in the Jam. Returns chronological sequence of: clicks, keyboard inputs, form submissions, navigation events, scroll actions, and other DOM interactions. The full timeline is returned by default and is small enough to read whole — pass limit only to cap the output, and page with `after` if a capped response reports a `nextCursor`. Invaluable for reproducing bugs and understanding user behavior patterns that triggered issues.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"jamId":{"type":"string","description":"Jam identifier — a UUID or a jam.dev URL"},"limit":{"type":"number","description":"Maximum number of events to return"},"after":{"type":"number","description":"Page cursor — pass the `nextCursor` from a previous response to continue"}},"required":["jamId"],"additionalProperties":false,"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#"},"eager_input_streaming":true,"defer_loading":true},{"name":"mcp__claude_ai_Jam__getVideoTranscript","description":"Retrieve the speech transcript (captions) from a video Jam recording in WebVTT format with timestamps. Only available for video Jams where the microphone was enabled during recording. Use this to understand what the user said while recording the bug report.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"jamId":{"type":"string","description":"Jam identifier — a UUID or a jam.dev URL"}},"required":["jamId"],"additionalProperties":false,"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#"},"eager_input_streaming":true,"defer_loading":true}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"d066daa7-9d72-4d9c-bf20-2c64e7f30130","timestamp":"2026-09-09T05:36:48.355Z","session_id":"21880ebb-4ca2-4b72-9b3d-3b6dba0010a6","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/jvent/Dev/supabase/supabase-devtool","sessionId":"21880ebb-4ca2-4b72-9b3d-3b6dba0010a6","version":"2.1.266","gitBranch":"main"}
